0003-condensate-na2o-al2o3-liquid-rows.patch
==========================================

Fixes two transcription defects in VapoRock's data/condensate-thermo-data.csv
(upstream https://gitlab.com/ENKI-portal/vaporock.git @ 0159678; applies on top of
0001 and 0002 of this series). Everything above the first `diff --git` line is a
note; `git apply` ignores it.

Scope and who is affected
-------------------------
VapoRock's own solver does not read this file: its oxide standard states come
from the MELTS liquid (src/vaporock/equil.py loads only vapor-thermo-data.csv and
the JANAF vapor CSVs), and no VapoRock Python code references
condensate-thermo-data.csv. The defects therefore do not change VapoRock's own
results. They do propagate to every consumer that copied the file as a
Lamoreaux liquid-oxide table, including the vendored IMCC-SF04 gas layer
(simulator/melt_backend/imcc_sf04/gas.py) and openimcc
(src/openimcc/data/gas/condensate.csv), where they set the Na and Al gas pressures.

Row format (as consumed by those gas layers)
--------------------------------------------
G(T) = R*1000*dH298_R - R*T*(dG_A + dG_B*t + dG_C*t^2 + dG_D*t^3 + dG_E*t^4),
t = T/1000. This is the Lamoreaux-Hildenbrand form
-(G_T - H_298)/(RT) = A + B*T + C*T^2 + D*T^3 (B, C, D scaled by 1e3/1e6/1e9 in the
printed tables), anchored on the 298.15 K formation enthalpy of the phase that is
stable at 298.15 K. LH84 p.153 states that transition enthalpies and entropies
are included in the tabulated functions at the transition temperature.

Defect 1: Na2O(l), line 7
-------------------------
  was: Na2O(l),l,Na,2,1,825,3000,-50.17,4.82,19.292,-5.267,0.623,0,LAM1984
  now: Na2O(l),l,Na,2,1,1405,3000,-50.17,7.67,6.193,0,0,0,LAM1984

The anchor -50.17 kK is correct: Lamoreaux & Hildenbrand (1984), Table 4, printed
p.157, Na2O(s) dfH298/R = -50.17 +/- 0.50 kK. The coefficients
(4.82, 19.292, -5.267, 0.623) and the 825 K lower bound belong to a different
species: they are LH84 Table 2 (printed p.154), row "NaO2(l)", 825-3000 K. The
Na2O(l) row of the same table is A = 7.67, 10^3 B = 6.193, 10^6 C = 0.000,
10^9 D = 0.000, 1405-3000 K. Table 1 (p.153) gives Na2O Tm = 1405 +/- 100 K.
- Effect: at 1900 K the wrong row makes Na2O(l) 92.1 kJ/mol too stable (101 kJ/mol
  at 2200 K) against JANAF Na-013 liquid, which puts p(Na) about 1.58 dex (x38) too
  low. With the correction, the Schaefer & Fegley (2004) Table 9 Na anchor at 1900 K
  goes from a -1.42 dex residual to +0.17 dex.
- Residual source difference, not part of this fix: corrected LH84 Na2O(l) is still
  less stable than JANAF Na-013 at every liquid node from 1600 to 3000 K: +13.4 kJ/mol
  at 1600 K, rising to +29.6 kJ/mol at 2400 K, and +17.7 kJ/mol at 3000 K.

Defect 2: Al2O3(l), line 4
--------------------------
  was: Al2O3(l),l,Al,2,3,2327,3000,-188.14,...,LAM1987
  now: Al2O3(l),l,Al,2,3,2327,3000,-201.54,...,LAM1987

-188.14 = -201.54 + 13.40. That is the Lamoreaux, Hildenbrand & Brewer (1987)
Table 3 Al2O3(s) anchor dfH298/R = -201.54 +/- 0.15 kK (printed p.424) with
the Table 1 fusion enthalpy dfusH/R = 13.40 +/- 0.36 kK added a second time. The
LH87 Table 2 (printed p.422) liquid function already carries the fusion terms at Tm = 2327 K, so
the anchor must be the solid value. The coefficients and the 2327-3000 K range are
correct as printed.
- Check: with -201.54, the row reproduces JANAF Al-100 liquid
  G = dfH298 + (H - H298) - T*S to within 0.1 kJ/mol at 2600-3000 K. With -188.14 it
  is off by a constant +111.4 kJ/mol, which puts p(Al), p(AlO) and p(Al2O) about
  1.3 dex too high at 2200 K (per Al atom).

Not changed (verified correct against the same tables)
------------------------------------------------------
K2O(l) (LH84 Table 2/4), MgO(l), CaO(l), SiO2(l), SiO2(cr) (LH87 Tables 1-3), and
FeO(l) (JANAF Fe-019). The Na2O(l) line carries a stray "-188.14" in an unnamed
trailing column, apparently a spreadsheet leftover; this patch leaves it untouched.

Sources
-------
- R. H. Lamoreaux, D. L. Hildenbrand, "High Temperature Vaporization Behavior of
  Oxides. I. Alkali Metal Binary Oxides", J. Phys. Chem. Ref. Data 13, 151 (1984),
  doi:10.1063/1.555706. Tables 1, 2 and 4, printed pp.153, 154 and 157.
  NIST reprint: https://srd.nist.gov/JPCRD/jpcrd241.pdf
  (sha256 3ecb3e3e9a5ee2487c92fdc185ef6b9e82d17c11bfe3e9969bb67abee943ba8a;
  scanned, no text layer; read visually).
- R. H. Lamoreaux, D. L. Hildenbrand, L. Brewer, "High-Temperature Vaporization
  Behavior of Oxides II. Oxides of Be, Mg, Ca, Sr, Ba, B, Al, Ga, In, Tl, Si, Ge,
  Sn, Pb, Zn, Cd, and Hg", J. Phys. Chem. Ref. Data 16, 419 (1987),
  doi:10.1063/1.555799. Tables 1-3, printed pp.421-424.
- NIST-JANAF 4th ed. tables Na-013 (Na2O liquid) and Al-100 (Al2O3 liquid).
- L. Schaefer, B. Fegley, Icarus 169, 216 (2004), doi:10.1016/j.icarus.2003.08.023,
  Tables 5 and 9 (Na check).

